      "title": "Adjunct, Athletic Training/Exercise Science",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct, Athletic Training/Exercise Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct, Athletic Training/Exercise Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are filled on an as needed basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct, Athletic Training/Exercise Science Job Description Adjunct faculty members to provide high-quality instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate courses within the Department of Physical Education, Sport and Human Performance in the Richard W. Riley College of Education, Sport, and Human Sciences. Teaching assignments may include Exercise Science, Health, Athletic Training, or other related disciplines and may be delivered in face-to-face, online, or hybrid formats. Position Responsibilities Teach assigned courses in accordance with approved course syllabi, departmental expectations, and university policies. Deliver engaging, student-centered instruction that supports course and program learning outcomes. Ensure course content, instructional activities, and assessments align with applicable accreditation standards and departmental expectations. Maintain regular communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments and assessments. Evaluate student performance fairly and maintain accurate course records. Submit grades and complete all required university reporting by established deadlines. Foster a professional, respectful, and inclusive learning environment. Respond promptly to departmental, college, and university communications and participate in required meetings and training as instructed. Comply with all university policies and procedures related to instruction, academic integrity, accessibility, and student privacy. About the College To learn more abo