    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/23220": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Basic Instruction",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct, Basic Instruction Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct, Basic Instruction Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are filled on an as needed basis for the 2026-2027 academic year. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct, Basic Instruction Job Description Adjunct basic instruction faculty members provide high-quality instruction in undergraduate physical activity courses within the Department of Physical Education, Sport and Human Performance in the Richard W. Riley College of Education, Sport, and Human Sciences. Position Responsibilities Teach assigned courses in accordance with approved course syllabi, departmental expectations, and university policies. Deliver engaging, student-centered instruction that supports course learning outcomes. Ensure course content, instructional activities, and assessments align with general education goals and departmental expectations. Maintain regular communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments and assessments. Evaluate student performance fairly and maintain accurate course records. Submit grades and complete all required university reporting by established deadlines. Foster a professional, respectful, and inclusive learning environment. Respond promptly to departmental, college, and university communications and participate in required meetings and training as requested. Comply with all university policies and procedures related to instruction, academic integrity, accessibility, and student privacy. About the College To learn more about the Richard W. Riley College of Education, Sport, and Human Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/ceshs/ . About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-